{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>After HaShem your Elohim you shall walk.</b> As in וְהָלַכְתָּ בִּדְרָכָיו (Deuteronomy 28:9) — and not in the ways that a prophet or dreamer may tell you, so as to seduce you from the way." "<b>And Him you shall fear.</b> Even if that prophet was already among you a man of importance and formidable stature and given to exaggeration, now you must nullify fear of the prophet for the sake of fear of El, blessed be He." "<b>And His commandments you shall keep.</b> And not new commandments that the prophet may innovate — especially regarding idolatry, which opposes all the commandments of El, exalted be He — for indeed He commanded לְעוֹלָם בְּרִיתוֹ, לֹא יַחֲלִיפֶנּוּ וְלֹא יָמִיר אוֹתוֹ (Psalms 111:9)." "<b>And to His voice you shall listen.</b> In what He desires through His prophets for the fulfillment of His Torah and the sanctification of His name — as in the case of Elijah on Mount Carmel — not to the voice of this one who nullifies all the commandments of El, exalted be He." "<b>And Him you shall serve.</b> Alone, as it says: זוֹבֵחַ לָאֱלֹהִים יָחֳרָם (Exodus 22:19), as was explained in its place." "<b>And to Him you shall cling.</b> That the end of all your actions be to do His will, and that your hatred [of the seducer] not be brought about by prior hatred."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:23.359658005Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}